x:"IP or CIDR",BlockPrefixPlaceholder:"203.0.113.8 or 2001:db8::/64",BlockDuration:"Duration",BlockReason:"Note",CloseExisting:"Close existing matching connections",OneHour:"1 hour",OneDay:"1 day",SevenDays:"7 days",Forever:"Permanent",ConfirmBlock:"Block source",NoConnections:"No matching connections",NoUDPActivity:"No matching UDP activity",Previous:"Previous",Next:"Next",PageSummary:"{total} total",Presets:"Protection preset",Strict:"Strict",StrictDesc:"For small hosts and management nodes exposed directly to the Internet.",Balanced:"Balanced",BalancedDesc:"Default balance between safety headroom and normal throughput.",HighThroughput:"High throughput",HighThroughputDesc:"Raises public budgets for controlled load tests or busy services; hard safeguards remain.",Custom:"Custom",BasicLimits:"Common limits",AdvancedLimits:"Advanced limits",WorkBudgets:"Work budgets",WorkBudgetsDesc:"Live TLS, request, outbound connection, and internal job usage",WorkBudgetsEditorDesc:"Shed work before entering expensive cryptography, parsing, proxy dialing, or process startup. Controlled load tests can raise the relevant budget; final resource safeguards remain active.",WorkReservations:"Work reservations",ReservedOfMax:"{reserved} reserved / {max} max",ConfigAdmissionInvalid:"Connection and work limits must be whole numbers; rate and burst must both be zero or both be positive.",ConfigPacketInvalid:"UDP packet size, rate, or burst is outside the safe range.",ConfigProbeInvalid:"Safe-entry probe rate, window, path count, or block duration is outside the safe range.",ConfigProtocolAbuseInvalid:"The Mux anomaly window, weighted event threshold, or auto-block duration is outside the safe range.",ConfigReservationInvalid:"Lifeline reservations violate a core invariant: critical admin, core, and tunnel slots must be at least one, public reservations must be zero, and totals must stay below their limits.",ConfigRateHeadroomInvalid:"The global rate or burst cannot cover all class budgets. Raise the global value or lower the public class so admin, core, and tunnel traffic retain token headroom.",ConfigStateInvalid:"State capacity is outside the safe range; UDP state capacity cannot be below the global UDP-session limit.",ConfigPressureInvalid:"CPU or goroutine thresholds are invalid; lifeline thresholds must exceed public thresholds.",ConfigUDPResponseInvalid:"UDP response amplification or initial response allowance is outside the safe range.",ConfigPrefixInvalid:"IPv4/IPv6 aggregate rules are invalid, duplicated, or too numerous; IPv6 must include a /64 rule.",ConfigCIDRInvalid:"A CIDR list contains an invalid prefix or more than 4,096 entries. Enter one address/prefix per line.",InvalidBlockTarget:"Enter a valid IP address or CIDR prefix.",TLSWork:"TLS handshakes",HTTPWork:"HTTP requests",AuthWork:"Authentication",WAFWork:"WAF checks",ParserWork:"Parsing",DecompressionWork:"Decompression and archive encoding",OutboundTCPWork:"Outbound TCP",TaskWork:"Internal tasks",FileWork:"File operations",TransferWork:"File transfer (64 KiB/credit)",StorageWork:"Storage operations",ProcessWork:"Child processes",TotalTCPMax:"Global TCP connections",PublicTCPMax:"Public TCP connections",TotalUDPMax:"Global UDP sessions",ClientTCPMax:"TCP connections per IP",ClientWorkMax:"Maximum work concurrency per IP",PrefixWorkBudgets:"Subnet work budgets",RequestRate:"Requests per IP / sec",AuthConcurrency:"Authentication concurrency",OutboundTCPConcurrency:"Outbound TCP concurrency",TaskConcurrency:"Internal tasks concurrency",ProbeRate:"Probe rate",ProbeUniquePaths:"Wrong paths",MuxAbuseWindow:"Window",MuxAbuseEvents:"Weighted-event threshold",StateCapacity:"Bounded state",IdentityCapacity:"Source-state capacity",UDPStateCapacity:"UDP-state capacity",LoginChallengeCapacity:"Login challenges total",PerIPChallengeCapacity:"Login challenges per IP",ProcessPressureGuard:"CPU and goroutine hard guard",ProcessPressureDesc:"The public threshold limits new public work while active transfers continue. Public and unauthenticated connections are closed only after CPU reaches the lifeline threshold for 2 seconds, or goroutines reach the lifeline threshold. Authenticated admin, core and tunnel-control connections are retained. The lifeline threshold also pauses new lifeline work until recovery. Protocol-abuse and source limits act independently. These hard guards remain active in observe mode.",PublicCPUPercent:"Public CPU threshold",LifelineCPUPercent:"Lifeline CPU threshold",PublicGoroutines:"Public goroutine threshold",LifelineGoroutines:"Lifeline goroutine threshold",UDPResponseGuard:"UDP egress & anti-amplification",UDPResponseDesc:"Responses require an admitted ingress session. The hard amplification ceiling applies until return routability is proven; verified peers still obey all egress packet/byte, endpoint, IP and prefix limits. Traffic is shown as in / out.",UDPMaxAmplification:"Pre-validation response amplification",UDPInitialBytes:"Initial handshake bytes",UDPInitialPackets:"Initial handshake packets",ProtocolGuard:"Protocol boundaries",SoftExemptions:"Soft-limit exemptions",SoftExemptionsDesc:"Bypasses only per-IP and prefix soft limits. Global capacity, bounded state, admin reserves, and final resource safeguards still apply.",TrustedProxies:"Trusted proxy / CDN CIDRs",TrustedProxiesSettingsHint:"Edit this under Settings → Connections & proxies → Global trusted proxy / CDN CIDRs. The saved configuration is shown here.",OpenGlobalSettings:"Open connections & proxies",TrustedProxiesDesc:"Only explicitly listed proxies are trusted. An empty list trusts no proxies; local proxies also require 127.0.0.1/32 or ::1/128 to be listed. Physical peers in these CIDRs bypass only IP/prefix soft limits, never global or resource hard guards. A CDN node is not auto-blocked before a trusted downstream identity is available; after PROXY identity binding, anomaly memory and limits apply to the real client. X-Forwarded-For is walked from the nearest hop to the first non-proxy address. Generic CIDR trust does not enable pass-through single-address headers.",CIDRPlaceholder:"One CIDR per line, for example 2001:db8::/32",SensitiveCIDRWarning:"These CIDRs change source identity or bypass per-source soft limits. A wrong range can let untrusted clients spoof forwarded identities or rotate identities; global capacity and resource hard guards still apply.",SensitiveCIDRTitle:"Confirm sensitive CIDR changes",SensitiveCIDRConfirm:"The trusted-proxy or soft-exemption list changed. Confirm that every range contains only a proxy/CDN you control or a source you intentionally exempt. Do not use 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 as a substitute for the high-throughput preset. Confirm and save?",SensitiveCIDRConfirmationStale:"The configuration changed while confirmation was open. Review it and save again so an earlier approval cannot authorize a new CIDR policy.",ConfirmAndSave:"Confirm and save",IPv4Policies:"IPv4 aggregate prefixes",IPv6Policies:"IPv6 hierarchical prefixes",Prefix:"Prefix",IPv6Required:"/64 is a core rule and cannot be removed. Wider prefixes such as /60, /56 and /48 stop clients from rotating addresses inside the same block.",CoverageFull:"Full",CoveragePartial:"Partial",CoverageReserved:"Reserved",CoverageUncovered:"Uncovered",CoverageSummary:"Coverage reflects real hooks. Third-party modules with only an outer fallback are never labeled fully protected.",EndpointCount:"{count} endpoints",Hooks:"Integrated",Gaps:"Remaining gaps",NoGaps:"No declared gaps",LoadingFailed:"Could not load ingress protection: {error}",Cancel:"Cancel",OperationFailed:"Operation failed",MutationAppliedRefreshFailed:"The change was applied, but live status could not be refreshed: {error}",LoadConnectionsFailed:"Could not load connections",ConnectionClosed:"Connection closed",UDPActivityCleared:"UDP activity state cleared",SourceBlocked:"Source blocked",Unblocked:"Block removed",CoreClass:"Core jobs",TunnelControlClass:"Tunnel control",ReasonBlockedPref